                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a 2022 overhaul of a 2018 game full of 2011 memes, with jokes ranging from \"epic!!\" to \"fatality lol\".\n\nGameplay is a bit primitive, lacking much depth to it (compared to, say, [url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/1120950/Chameleon_Run_Deluxe_Edition/]Chameleon Run[/url]) even for an auto-runner. You can choose a helper item at the beginning of the stage (such as double-jump or extra life) but those are one-time use consumables. You lose them upon death but they cost a LOT of in-game coins to purchase (several full minutes worth of farming just to buy one). It's not good design honestly, and wasting items on random deaths is frustrating so you end up just not using them at all.\n\nStill, it's a decent time killer and obtaining 100% achievements took some effort. I'd put a Mixed review if Steam would allow me.",
